  "coverage": {
    "complete": true,
    "lastDateReached": "2027-06-12",
    "why": "The site's own /events/filtered/<year>/<month> pages were fetched for every month from Sep 2026 through Jun 2027 (Jun fetched to confirm no events beyond scope's May 31 cutoff were missed). Three of those ten month-pages (Sep 2026, Oct 2026, May 2027) returned HTTP 406 from curl on every retry -- consistent with the site's WAF, not a real absence of a page -- and were re-fetched via firecrawl_scrape instead, which succeeded. Listing pages give date, venue room, title, event URL, and a status/on-sale button; they do NOT carry support-act billing, exact showtime, or the outbound ticket-seller URL (AXS, based on one spot-checked detail page) for most rows -- those live only on each event's own /event/... detail page, and that path also returned 406 under curl. One detail page was fetched via firecrawl as a spot check; the remaining 98 were not, to stay inside the firecrawl call budget for the whole 5-venue task. 'time' below is read from the venue's own URL slug (e.g. '.../-at-8-pm', which the venue's CMS generates from the real showtime), not inferred by me. One event (Alison Krauss & Union Station, cancelled) is omitted from the events list because the site prints its date as literal 'TBD' with no reschedule date -- noted here rather than guessed."
  },
